Subject: wayland: run where the compositor has no zphoc_device_state_v1

Stevia asks the compositor for phoc's device-state protocol (is a hardware
keyboard attached?) and counts it among the globals it can't do without, so
on a compositor without it the keyboard never becomes ready. Hyprland doesn't
have it. The protocol is now optional: without it there is no hardware
keyboard tracking, and everything else works.
---
--- a/src/pos-hw-tracker.c
+++ b/src/pos-hw-tracker.c
@@ -72,6 +72,9 @@
                                  gpointer      device_state)
 {
   self->device_state = device_state;
+  /* Not every compositor has it (Hyprland): no hardware keyboard tracking then */
+  if (!self->device_state)
+    return;
   zphoc_device_state_v1_add_listener (self->device_state, &device_state_listener, self);
 }
 
--- a/src/pos-wayland.c
+++ b/src/pos-wayland.c
@@ -387,6 +387,5 @@
           self->zwlr_foreign_toplevel_manager_v1 &&
           self->layer_shell &&
           self->zxdg_output_manager_v1 &&
-          self->zphoc_device_state_v1 &&
           self->ext_data_control_manager);
 }
